 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Lovely. small blanket each one can huddle under, with a few small toys, and some yummy sandwiches. Sure, I'd be glad to help. Which end is up, and which down? Roughly which way is your back, so it' whichever end is towards you when you' turning your back to it, and which way is down is whichever end is at the bottom. Load it on the back with the hole at the top, so it stays flat. Then push it down a bit with your foot, then tilt it up. Some kids do, it makes it easier for one person to move it. Then get him to push, you hold the handle, and see if he can turn it one layer at a time.",
